@startuml SEQ-10-IdempotentCreate
' POST /requests retried after a timeout — the stored response is replayed (README 3.2, ADR-010).
actor Solicitante
participant "IdempotencyService" as IDEM
participant "PurchaseRequestService" as S
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== First attempt ==
Solicitante -> IDEM : POST /requests (key=K, payload=P) — the response is lost
IDEM -> DB : BEGIN; INSERT idempotency_keys … ON CONFLICT … RETURNING (1 row: reserved)
IDEM -> S : create(actor, P)
S -> DB : INSERT purchase_requests + items + event
IDEM -> DB : UPDATE idempotency_keys SET response (201, body R); COMMIT
IDEM --> Solicitante : (lost in the network)

== Retry: same key, same payload ==
Solicitante -> IDEM : POST /requests (key=K, payload=P)
IDEM -> DB : SELECT → live record, hash matches
IDEM --> Solicitante : 201, body R, Idempotent-Replayed: true — no new request

== Concurrent duplicate ==
Solicitante -> IDEM : POST /requests (key=K, payload=P)   [while the first is still running]
IDEM -> DB : INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE WHERE expires_at < now()\n→ waits on the PK; winner commits → 0 rows (no error)
IDEM -> DB : ROLLBACK; SELECT winner's record → replay R

== Same key, different payload ==
Solicitante -> IDEM : POST /requests (key=K, payload=P')
IDEM -> DB : SELECT → hash mismatch
IDEM --> Solicitante : 409 IDEMPOTENCY_PAYLOAD_MISMATCH
note over IDEM,DB : the payload hash is SHA-256 of a canonical form (prices in cents);\nexpired keys are taken over by the same INSERT and purged by IdempotencyPurgeJob
@enduml
